searchDatas1[11] = ['','Overview','./overview.html', '	Overview	Network Setup Tool for fi Series is an application that is used to connect an fi Series image scanner to a network to make the scanner available.	Network Setup Tool for fi Series comes with the following tools.	The supported scanner models vary depending on the tool that is used for the model. Check that the name of your scanner model that you are using is one of the names of the scanner models that are supported by each tool in advance. For details about scanner models supported by each tool, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.	Scanner Selection Tool	This tool is for selecting a scanner that you want to use from a computer.	You can select a single scanner among scanners connected to a network.	When you select fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8040, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250, you can also perform the following operations.	Start up fi Series Network Settings (on a web browser) from the [Scanner Selection Tool] window to configure the scanner settings	Start up Software Operation Panel from your computer to configure the scanner settings	For details about fi Series Network Settings (on a web browser) and Software Operation Panel, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	IP Address Setting Tool	This tool is for setting an IP address, scanner name, security related information, and other network information.	Certificate Registration Tool	This is a tool to register a certificate on a scanner to connect the scanner to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi.	After registering a certificate on the scanner, configure the Wi-Fi settings on the touch screen of the scanner.	Certificates that can be registered are as follows:	Client certificate: PKCS#12 format file (*.p12, *.pfx)	CA certificate: CA certificate file (*.cer, *.crt, *.der, *.pem)	Button Event Manager	This is a tool to specify an image scanning application that you want to start up when a button on a scanner is pressed.	You need to use Scanner Selection Tool to set a scanner connected to a network to be able to use it on a computer.	'];
searchDatas1[12] = ['','Flow of the Operation','./flow.html', '	Flow of the Operation	The following shows the flow of the operation for using an image scanning application in order to scan documents. 	Starting a scan from an image scanning application	Starting a scan by running an image scanning application from the button on a scanner	Starting a scan from an image scanning application	For fi-8040 or fi-7300NX	Configure the network settings on the touch screen of the scanner	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Connect the scanner to a network	TIP	When you use fi-7300NX connected to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi, the certificate must be registered on the scanner in advance. For details, refer to 	Registering Certificates on a Scanner.	Start up Scanner Selection Tool to select the scanner that you want to use from a computer	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use.	In an image scanning application, select the scanner connected to a wired LAN or Wi-Fi	Names of the scanners connected to a wired LAN or Wi-Fi are as follows:	For PaperStream IP (TWAIN)/PaperStream IP (TWAIN x64)	PaperStream IP xxx Net	For PaperStream IP (ISIS) fi-8000 series/PaperStream IP (ISIS) Bundle	PaperStream_IP xxx Net	"xxx" indicates the scanner model name. For details, refer to the Help of the scanner driver.	TIP	Only fi-7300NX can be used with a Wi-Fi connection.	Load documents in a scanner and scan them from an image scanning application	For details about how to load documents, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	TIP	Even though a scanner is selected with Scanner Selection Tool, the scanner may not appear in the image scanning application that is being used. For details, refer to 	Cannot Perform a Scan from the Image Scanning Application.	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250	Connect a scanner to a network device (such as a switch, hub, or router) with a LAN cable	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	When an IP address is automatically assigned	Proceed to the next step.	When you assign an IP address manually	Start up IP Address Setting Tool to assign an IP address to a scanner.	For details, refer to 	Changing the IP Address for a Scanner.	Start up Scanner Selection Tool to select the scanner that you want to use from a computer	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use.	In an image scanning application, select the scanner connected to a wired LAN	Names of the scanners connected to a wired LAN are as follows:	For PaperStream IP (TWAIN)/PaperStream IP (TWAIN x64)	PaperStream IP xxx Net	For PaperStream IP (ISIS) fi-8000 series	PaperStream_IP xxx Net	"xxx" indicates the scanner model name. For details, refer to the Help of the scanner driver.	Load documents in a scanner and scan them from an image scanning application	For details about how to load documents, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	TIP	Even though a scanner is selected with Scanner Selection Tool, the scanner may not appear in the image scanning application that is being used. For details, refer to 	Cannot Perform a Scan from the Image Scanning Application.	Starting a scan by running an image scanning application from the button on a scanner	For fi-8040 or fi-7300NX	Configure the network settings on the touch screen of the scanner	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Connect the scanner to a network	TIP	When you use fi-7300NX connected to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi, the certificate must be registered on the scanner in advance. For details, refer to 	Registering Certificates on a Scanner.	Start up Scanner Selection Tool to select the scanner that you want to use from a computer	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use.	Start up Button Event Manager and specify an image scanning application to be started when the button on the scanner is pressed	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner.	ATTENTION	When the same scanner has been selected by more than one computer using Scanner Selection Tool, select [Watch Button Event] on the menu of Button Event Manager only on the computer that you want to use the scanner with.	Load documents in the scanner, and press the button on the scanner to scan the documents	For details about how to load documents, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250	Connect a scanner to a network device (such as a switch, hub, or router) with a LAN cable	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	When an IP address is automatically assigned	Proceed to the next step.	When you assign an IP address manually	Start up IP Address Setting Tool to assign an IP address to a scanner.	For details, refer to 	Changing the IP Address for a Scanner.	Start up Scanner Selection Tool to select the scanner that you want to use from a computer	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use.	Start up Button Event Manager and specify an image scanning application to be started when the button on the scanner is pressed	For details, refer to step 3 and the subsequent steps in 	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner.	ATTENTION	When the same scanner has been selected by more than one computer using Scanner Selection Tool, select [Watch Button Event] on the menu of Button Event Manager only on the computer that you want to use the scanner with.	Load documents in the scanner, and press the button on the scanner to scan the documents	For details about how to load documents, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[13] = ['','Start-up','./title_startup.html', '	Start-up	This section explains how to start each tool in Network Setup Tool for fi Series.	The supported scanner models vary depending on the tool that is used for the model. For details about scanner models supported by each tool, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.	Starting Up Scanner Selection Tool	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool	Starting Up Certificate Registration Tool	Starting Up Button Event Manager	'];
searchDatas1[14] = ['','Starting Up Scanner Selection Tool','./startup_select.html', '	Starting Up Scanner Selection Tool	This section explains how to start up Scanner Selection Tool. 	Start-up procedure	For Windows 10/Windows Server 2016/Windows Server 2019/Windows Server 2022	Select [Start] menu 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Scanner Selection Tool for fi Series].	For Windows 11/Windows Server 2025	Select [Start] menu 	→ [All apps] 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Scanner Selection Tool for fi Series].	TIP	You can also start Scanner Selection Tool by clicking the [Select a Scanner] button in the [IP Address Setting Tool] window.'];
searchDatas1[15] = ['','Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool','./startup_ipaddress.html', '	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool	This section explains how to start up IP Address Setting Tool. 	Start-up procedure	For Windows 10/Windows Server 2016/Windows Server 2019/Windows Server 2022	Select [Start] menu 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [IP Address Setting Tool for fi Series].	For Windows 11/Windows Server 2025	Select [Start] menu 	→ [All apps] 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [IP Address Setting Tool for fi Series].	TIP	You can also start IP Address Setting Tool by clicking the [Set an IP Address] button in the [Scanner Selection Tool] window.'];
searchDatas1[16] = ['','Starting Up Certificate Registration Tool','./startup_cer.html', '	Starting Up Certificate Registration Tool	This section explains how to start up Certificate Registration Tool. 	Start-up procedure	For Windows 10/Windows Server 2016/Windows Server 2019/Windows Server 2022	Select [Start] menu 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Certificate Registration Tool for fi Series].	For Windows 11/Windows Server 2025	Select [Start] menu 	→ [All apps] 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Certificate Registration Tool for fi Series].'];
searchDatas1[17] = ['','Starting Up Button Event Manager','./startup_buttoneventmanager.html', '	Starting Up Button Event Manager	This section explains how to start up Button Event Manager. 	Start-up procedure	For Windows 10/Windows Server 2016/Windows Server 2019/Windows Server 2022	Select [Start] menu 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Button Event Manager for fi Series].	For Windows 11/Windows Server 2025	Select [Start] menu 	→ [All apps] 	→ [fi Series] 	→ [Button Event Manager for fi Series].	TIP	When Button Event Manager is started, 	 appears in the notification area located at the far right at the bottom of the task bar notifying you of a message.'];
searchDatas1[18] = ['','Operations','./title_ope.html', '	Operations	This section explains how to use each tool in Network Setup Tool for fi Series.	The supported scanner models vary depending on the tool that is used for the model. For details about scanner models supported by each tool, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.	ATTENTION	When the scanner is in the middle of a scan, settings cannot be configured from Scanner Selection Tool, IP Address Setting Tool, and Certificate Registration Tool.	Scanner Selection Tool	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use	IP Address Setting Tool	Changing the Scanner Name	Changing the IP Address for a Scanner	Encrypting Communications on the Network	Certificate Registration Tool	Register a Certificate	Remove a Certificate	Button Event Manager	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use	Changing the Network Settings of a Scanner	Registering Certificates on a Scanner	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner	'];
searchDatas1[19] = ['','Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use','./opr_cnf_scanner.html', '	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use	This section explains how to use Scanner Selection Tool in order to select a scanner that you want to use from a computer. 	Connect a scanner to a network. 	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Start up Scanner Selection Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up Scanner Selection Tool.	The 	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window appears.	TIP	When you start Scanner Selection Tool, this tool automatically searches for scanners within the search range that is set for [Search Method for the Scanner].	From the scanner list, select the scanner that you want to use from a computer. 	A check mark appears next to a selected scanner.	TIP	If the scanner that you want to use is not shown in the scanner list, search for the scanner in the following procedure.	When the scanner is connected to the same subnetwork as the one that the computer is connected to	Select [IPv4] or [IPv6] in [Search Range] under [Search Method for the Scanner], and click the [Search again] button	When the scanner is connected to a different subnetwork from the one that the computer is connected to	Select [Enter an IP address] or [Enter a name] in [Search Range] under [Search Method for the Scanner], and enter the IP address or the name, and click the [Search again] button	Click the [OK] button. 	TIP	You can also double-click a scanner in the scanner list to select the scanner.	Double-clicking the scanner makes the scanner available for a computer and exits Scanner Selection Tool.	When you specify [Enter an IP address] or [Enter a name] in [Search Range] under [Search Method for the Scanner], check that an IP address or a name is entered in the input field, then click the [OK] button.	See also	No Scanner Is Found'];
searchDatas1[20] = ['','Changing the Network Settings of a Scanner','./opr_change_nw.html', '	Changing the Network Settings of a Scanner	Use IP Address Setting Tool to change the network settings of a scanner. 	TIP	You can also use fi Series Network Settings (on a web browser) to change the network settings of a scanner. For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Changing the Scanner Name	Changing the IP Address for a Scanner	Encrypting Communications on the Network	'];
searchDatas1[21] = ['','Changing the Scanner Name','./opr_scanner_name.html', '	Changing the Scanner Name	This section explains how to use IP Address Setting Tool in order to change the scanner name.	The scanner name is displayed in the scanner list in the [Scanner Selection Tool] window.	The factory default setting for the scanner name is the model name and the serial number of the scanner (Model name - Serial number).	The serial number of the scanner is printed on the product label.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Connect a scanner to a computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner. 	Turn on the scanner. 	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Start up IP Address Setting Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.	The login window of IP Address Setting Tool appears.	When an administrator password is not set for the scanner, the 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears. Proceed to step 5.	Enter the administrator password for a scanner, and click the [Login] button. 	For details about the factory default administrator password, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	The 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears.	Enter appropriate characters in [Scanner Name]. 	Available characters are alphanumeric characters, "-" (hyphen), "_" (underscore), and spaces.	Up to 64 characters can be set.	TIP	If you enable [Dynamic DNS] in the scanner settings, enter a scanner name with a length of 63 characters or less.	For details about Dynamic DNS, refer to the Operator\'s Guide for the scanner.	It is recommended that you not use the following half-width characters when registering a scanner name on the DNS server because the characters will be converted to "-" (hyphen).	_ (Underscore)	Spaces	Click the [OK] button. 	Unplug the USB cable from the scanner. '];
searchDatas1[22] = ['','Changing the IP Address for a Scanner','./opr_ip_set.html', '	Changing the IP Address for a Scanner	This section explains how to use IP Address Setting Tool to change the IP address for a scanner.	The IP address is displayed in the scanner list in the [Scanner Selection Tool] window.	The IPv4 address or IPv6 address is assigned automatically to a scanner as the factory default setting.	For example, use IP Address Setting Tool to change the IP address of a scanner in the following cases.	When a scanner is not found in Scanner Selection Tool	When connecting a scanner to a network that does not use a DHCP server	When you want to set a fixed IP address for a scanner	Connect a scanner to a computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner. 	Turn on the scanner. 	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Start up IP Address Setting Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.	The login window of IP Address Setting Tool appears.	When an administrator password is not set for the scanner, the 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears. Proceed to step 5.	Enter the administrator password for a scanner, and click the [Login] button. 	For details about the factory default administrator password, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	The 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears.	Select a method to set an IP address. 	IPv4 address	Select a method to set an IP address for a scanner in [IPv4 Configuration] under [Network].	When you select [Auto]	Proceed to step 6.	When you select [Manual]	Enter appropriate numbers in [IP Address], [Subnet Mask], and [Default Gateway].	IPv6 address	Click the [IPv6 Settings] button in [IPv6] under [Network].	Select a method to set an IP address for a scanner in [IPv6 Configuration] in the 	[IPv6 Settings] Window.	When you select [Auto] or [Disable]	Click the [OK] button, and proceed to step 6.	When you select [Manual]	Enter appropriate numbers in [IP Address], [Subnet prefix length], and [Default Gateway].	Click the [OK] button.	Click the [OK] button. 	Unplug the USB cable from the scanner. '];
searchDatas1[23] = ['','Encrypting Communications on the Network','./opr_encryption.html', '	Encrypting Communications on the Network	This section explains how to use IP Address Setting Tool in order to encrypt communications on the network. 	Connect a scanner to a computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner. 	Turn on the scanner. 	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Start up IP Address Setting Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.	The login window of IP Address Setting Tool appears.	When an administrator password is not set for the scanner, the 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears. Proceed to step 5.	Enter the administrator password for a scanner, and click the [Login] button. 	For details about the factory default administrator password, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	The 	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window appears.	Select [Encryption On (HTTPS)] for [Network Encryption] in [Security]. 	Click the [OK] button. '];
searchDatas1[24] = ['','Registering Certificates on a Scanner','./opr_cer.html', '	Registering Certificates on a Scanner	Use Certificate Registration Tool to register a certificate on a scanner or remove an unnecessary certificate when you connect the scanner to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi. 	Register a Certificate	Remove a Certificate	'];
searchDatas1[25] = ['','Register a Certificate','./opr_cer_reg.html', '	Register a Certificate	This section explains how to use Certificate Registration Tool to register a certificate on a scanner.	To connect a scanner to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi , register this certificate on the scanner in advance.	Certificates that can be registered are as follows:	Client certificate: PKCS#12 format file (*.p12, *.pfx)	CA certificate: CA certificate file (*.cer, *.crt, *.der, *.pem)	Start up Certificate Registration Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up Certificate Registration Tool.	The 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window appears.	Connect a scanner to a computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner, and click the [Set] button in the [Certificate Registration Tool] window. 	The 	Certificate Settings Window appears.	ATTENTION	If you disconnect then connect the USB cable while the certificate settings window is displayed, you cannot register a certificate.	Close the certificate settings window, and click the [Set] button again in the [Certificate Registration Tool] window.	Select a tab for the certificate that you want to register ([Client Certificates] or [CA Certificates]) and click the [Register] button. 	When the [Client Certificates] tab is selected, the 	[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates) appears.	When [CA Certificates] tab is selected, the 	[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates) appears.	Specify a certificate that you want to register. 	To register a client certificate, enter a password for the certificate.	Click the [OK] button. 	The certificate is registered on the scanner.	The certificate is added to a tab for the certificate ([Client Certificates] or [CA Certificates]) in the certificate settings window.	Click the [OK] button. 	Unplug the USB cable from the scanner. 	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again. 	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.'];
searchDatas1[26] = ['','Remove a Certificate','./opr_cer_del.html', '	Remove a Certificate	This section explains how to use Certificate Registration Tool to remove a certificate that has been registered on the scanner. 	Start up Certificate Registration Tool. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up Certificate Registration Tool.	The 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window appears.	Connect a scanner to a computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner, and click the [Set] button in the [Certificate Registration Tool] window. 	The 	Certificate Settings Window appears.	ATTENTION	If you disconnect then connect the USB cable while the certificate settings window is displayed, you cannot remove a certificate.	Close the certificate settings window, and click the [Set] button again in the [Certificate Registration Tool] window.	Select a tab for the certificate that you want to remove ([Client Certificates] or [CA Certificates]). 	Select a certificate that you want to remove. 	Click the [Remove] button. 	The certificate is removed from the scanner.	Click the [OK] button. 	Unplug the USB cable from the scanner. 	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again. 	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.'];
searchDatas1[27] = ['','Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner','./opr_buttonevent.html', '	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner	This section explains how to use Button Event Manager and specify an image scanning application to be started when a button on a scanner is pressed.	ATTENTION	When the same scanner has been selected by more than one computer using Scanner Selection Tool, select [Watch Button Event] on the menu of Button Event Manager only on the computer that you want to use the scanner with.	TIP	If you use Button Event Manager to specify an image scanning application for the scan button on a scanner, take note of the following.	When PaperStream ClickScan is running	Regardless of any settings that were configured for the scan button with Button Event Manager, a scan is performed with PaperStream ClickScan when the scan button on a scanner is pressed.	To start up another image scanning application (by pressing the scan button on a scanner), exit PaperStream ClickScan. For details, refer to the PaperStream ClickScan Help.	When PaperStream ClickScan is not running and PaperStream Capture is installed	PaperStream Capture is automatically set for the scan button on a scanner.	If you do not set PaperStream Capture for the scan button on a scanner, select [Take no action] or [Run the following program] for [Operation] in the 	[Button Settings] Window.	Connect a scanner to a network. 	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Enable the scanner to be selected in an image scanning application. 	Start up Scanner Selection Tool, and select the scanner to be used from scanners connected to a network.	For details, refer to 	Selecting a Scanner That You Want to Use.	Configure the scan settings in the image scanning application. 	For details, refer to the manual for the image scanning application.	Start up Button Event Manager. 	For details, refer to 	Starting Up Button Event Manager.	When Button Event Manager is started, 	 appears in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar.	Right-click 	. 	The 	Menu of Button Event Manager appears.	Select [Watch Button Event] on the menu. 	Click [Configure button settings] on the menu. 	The 	[Button Settings] Window appears.	Specify an image scanning application to be started when a button on a scanner is pressed. 	For details about the settings, refer to 	[Button Settings] Window.	Click the [OK] button. '];
searchDatas1[28] = ['','Windows','./title_window.html', '	Windows	This section describes the window for each tool in Network Setup Tool for fi Series.	The supported scanner models vary depending on the tool that is used for the model. For details about scanner models supported by each tool, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.	Scanner Selection Tool	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window	IP Address Setting Tool	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window	[IPv6 Settings] Window	Certificate Registration Tool	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window	Certificate Settings Window	[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates)	[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates)	[Details of the Certificate] Window	Button Event Manager	Menu of Button Event Manager	[Button Settings] Window	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window	Menu of Button Event Manager	'];
searchDatas1[29] = ['','[Scanner Selection Tool] Window','./dbox_select.html', '	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window	From among the scanners connected to a network, select a scanner that you want to use from your computer. 	Do you want to operate a scanner from an application? 	Displays the help.	Scanner list 	Displays the information of scanners that are found.	When you start Scanner Selection Tool, this tool automatically searches for scanners within the search range that is set for [Search Method for the Scanner], and displays model names, scanner names as well as IP addresses of scanners that are found.	Click the name of a scanner that you want to use from your computer in order to select the check box. You can select only one scanner.	If a scanner has already been selected, the scanner appears at the top of the scanner list.	When you do not use a scanner that is connected to the network, click the name of the selected scanner to clear the check mark.	TIP	You can also double-click a scanner in the scanner list to select the scanner.	Double-clicking the scanner makes the scanner available for a computer and exits Scanner Selection Tool.	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8040, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250, clicking an IP address displayed in [IP Address] on the scanner list starts up fi Series Network Settings (on a web browser).	For details about fi Series Network Settings (on a web browser), refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	When a scanner has already been selected and you start Scanner Selection Tool or click the [Search again] button in the [Scanner Selection Tool] window in one of the following states, 	 will be added to the selected scanner instead of 	.	The selected scanner is not connected to a network 	The selected scanner is turned off 	A value that will not search the selected scanner has been specified in [Search Range] under [Search Method for the Scanner]	In this case, if the selected scanner is connected to a network, you can use the scanner as is.	Search Method for the Scanner 	Search Range 	IPv4 	Searches for scanners that are connected to the same subnetwork as your computer using an IPv4 address.	This is the factory default setting.	IPv6 	Searches for scanners that are connected to the same subnetwork as your computer using an IPv6 address.	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8040, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250, you can select this to search for scanners.	Enter an IP address 	Select this to search for a scanner by specifying the IP address of a scanner or select this in order to use a scanner connected to a subnetwork that is different from the subnetwork which your computer is connected to.	Enter an IP address in the input fields.	Enter a name 	Select this to search for a scanner by specifying the name of a scanner which is registered on the DNS server.	TIP	The name of a scanner must be a name that is registered on the DNS server.	Enter a name within 255 characters in the input field.	The following characters are available:	Alphanumeric characters	- (Hyphen)	. (Period)	[Search again] button 	Starts a search for a scanner.	Could you not find the scanner you are looking for? 	Displays the help.	[Set an IP Address] button 	Start up IP Address Setting Tool.	When the scanner that you want to use from your computer is not found, clicking this allows you to check the scanner name or the IP address of the scanner.	To use IP Address Setting Tool, you need to connect the scanner to your computer via the USB cable.	[OK] button 	Exits Scanner Selection Tool.	The changes are saved.	[Cancel] button 	Exits Scanner Selection Tool.	The changes are not saved.'];
searchDatas1[30] = ['','[IP Address Setting Tool] Window','./dbox_ip_set.html', '	[IP Address Setting Tool] Window	Change the network settings of a scanner. 	Scanner Name 	Enter a scanner name within 64 characters.	The following characters are available:	Alphanumeric characters	- (Hyphen)	_ (Underscore)	Spaces	Note that spaces at the beginning and end of a name are deleted.	The factory default setting is the model name and the serial number of the scanner (Model name - Serial number).	TIP	The serial number of the scanner is printed on the product label.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	If you enable [Dynamic DNS] in the scanner settings, enter a scanner name with a length of 63 characters or less.	For details about Dynamic DNS, refer to the Operator\'s Guide for the scanner.	It is recommended that you not use the following half-width characters when registering a scanner name on the DNS server because the characters will be converted to "-" (hyphen).	_ (Underscore)	Spaces	Network 	Displays the network settings for a scanner.	MAC Address 	Displays the MAC address of a scanner.	IPv4 	IPv4 Configuration 	Select a method to set an IPv4 address for a scanner.	Auto	An IP address is automatically assigned to a scanner from the DHCP server.	This is the factory default setting.	Manual	Assign an IP address manually.	IP Address 	Displays the IP address of a scanner.	Enter an IP address for a scanner when you select [Manual] in [IPv4 Configuration].	Subnet Mask 	Displays the subnet mask for the IP address.	Enter a subnet mask for the IP address when you select [Manual] in [IPv4 Configuration].	Default Gateway 	Displays the default gateway for the IP address.	Enter a default gateway for the IP address when you select [Manual] in [IPv4 Configuration].	IPv6 	IP Address 	Displays the IP address and subnet prefix length of a scanner.	Default Gateway 	Displays the default gateway for the IP address.	[IPv6 Settings] button 	Displays the 	[IPv6 Settings] Window.	Set an IPv6 address.	Security 	Network Encryption 	Specify whether to encrypt network communications.	Encryption Off (HTTP) 	This is a transmission method prioritizing the scanning speed.	This is the factory default setting.	Encryption On (HTTPS) 	This is a transmission method prioritizing the security.	Note that the scanning speed may slow down.	Do you want to operate a scanner from an application? 	Displays the help.	[Select a Scanner] button 	Start up Scanner Selection Tool.	TIP	To use a scanner connected to a network from a computer, you need to use Scanner Selection Tool in order to select the scanner.	[OK] button 	Exits IP Address Setting Tool.	The changes are saved.	[Cancel] button 	Exits IP Address Setting Tool.	The changes are not saved.	[Apply] button 	The changes are saved.	[IPv6 Settings] Window	'];
searchDatas1[31] = ['','[IPv6 Settings] Window','./dbox_ipv6_set.html', '	[IPv6 Settings] Window	Set an IPv6 address. 	IPv6 Configuration 	Select a method to set an IPv6 address for a scanner.	Auto	An IP address is automatically assigned to a scanner from the DHCP server.	This is the factory default setting.	Manual	Assign an IP address manually.	Disable	Disable the IPv6 address settings.	[Receive RA packet] check box 	This check box appears when you select [Manual] in [IPv6 Configuration].	Select this to enable an IPv6 address that has been generated automatically.	You can check an IPv6 address that has been generated automatically in [IP Address] under [IPv6] in the [IP Address Setting Tool] window.	The check box is selected for the factory default setting.	IP Address 	Enter an IP address for a scanner when you select [Manual] in [IPv6 Configuration].	Subnet prefix length 	Enter a subnet prefix length for the IP address when you select [Manual] in [IPv6 Configuration].	A value from 3 to 128 can be entered.	Default Gateway 	Enter a default gateway for the IP address when you select [Manual] in [IPv6 Configuration].	[OK] button 	Closes the window.	The changes are applied to the [IP Address Setting Tool] window.	[Cancel] button 	Closes the window.	The changes are not applied to the [IP Address Setting Tool] window.'];
searchDatas1[32] = ['','[Certificate Registration Tool] Window','./dbox_cer.html', '	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window	Register a certificate on a scanner or remove an unnecessary certificate when you connect the scanner to a network that requires a certificate via Wi-Fi. 	[Set] button 	Clicking this button displays the 	Certificate Settings Window.	[Close] button 	Exits Certificate Registration Tool.	Certificate Settings Window	[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates)	[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates)	[Details of the Certificate] Window	'];
searchDatas1[33] = ['','Certificate Settings Window','./dbox_cer_cnf.html', '	Certificate Settings Window	A client certificate and a CA certificate can be set. 	[Client Certificates] tab/[CA Certificates] tab 	Select one of them according to the certificate that you want to register or remove.	When a certificate is registered, the information of the certificate is displayed.	[Register] button 	Registers certificates on the scanner.	One certificate for each certificate type can be registered on the scanner.	If certificates are already registered, the existing certificates are overwritten.	When the [Client Certificates] tab is selected, the 	[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates) appears.	When [CA Certificates] tab is selected, the 	[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates) appears.	[Details] button 	Displays detailed information of the registered certificates on the scanner.	Clicking this button displays the 	[Details of the Certificate] Window.	[Remove] button 	Removes a certificate registered on the scanner.	[Back] button 	Returns to the 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window.'];
searchDatas1[34] = ['','[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates)','./dbox_cer_reg_client.html', '	[Certificate Registration] Window (Client Certificates)	A client certificate can be registered on a scanner. 	File name of the Client Certificate (PKCS #12 format) 	Enter a file name of the certificate that you register.	[Browse] button 	Specify a file of the certificate that you register.	Clicking this button displays the [Select a Client Certificate] window.	Password 	Enter the password.	[OK] button 	Registers the certificate on the scanner and closes the window.	[Cancel] button 	Closes the window.'];
searchDatas1[35] = ['','[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates)','./dbox_cer_reg_ca.html', '	[Certificate Registration] Window (CA Certificates)	A CA certificate can be registered on a scanner. 	File Name of the CA Certificate 	Enter a file name of the certificate that you register.	[Browse] button 	Specify a file of the certificate that you register.	Clicking this button displays the [Select a CA Certificate] window.	[OK] button 	Registers the certificate on the scanner and closes the window.	[Cancel] button 	Closes the window.'];
searchDatas1[36] = ['','[Details of the Certificate] Window','./dbox_cer_detail.html', '	[Details of the Certificate] Window	The information of the registered certificates on the scanner is displayed. 	The information of the following items appears.	Version	Serial Number	Signature Algorithm	Issuer	Valid from	Valid until	Subject	Public Key	[OK] button 	Closes the window.'];
searchDatas1[37] = ['','Menu of Button Event Manager','./dbox_buttoneventmanager.html', '	Menu of Button Event Manager	The following menu items are displayed when you right-click 	 in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar. 	Watch Button Event 	Detects the downward motion of a button on a scanner.	If this is not selected, an image scanning application that you specified in the 	[Button Settings] Window is not started when the button on the scanner is pressed.	ATTENTION	When the same scanner has been selected by more than one computer using Scanner Selection Tool, select [Watch Button Event] only on the computer that you want to use the scanner with.	TIP	To start up the Software Operation Panel by pressing the scan button on the scanner, select [Watch Button Event].	For details about how a scanner operates (functions) when the scan button on the scanner is pressed, refer to the Operator\'s Guide for the scanner.	Launch this tool when logging on 	If this is selected, Button Event Manager is launched when signing in to Windows.	When Button Event Manager is started, a notification message appears in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar.	Configure button settings 	Specify an image scanning application to be started when a button on a scanner is pressed.	The 	[Button Settings] Window appears.	Help 	Displays the help.	About 	Displays the version information.	Exit 	Exits Button Event Manager.	[Button Settings] Window	'];
searchDatas1[38] = ['','[Button Settings] Window','./dbox_buttonevent.html', '	[Button Settings] Window	Specify an image scanning application that you want to start up when a button on a scanner is pressed. 	Select an event 	From the button list, select a button to specify an image scanning application to be started up when a button on a scanner is pressed.	TIP	The button names shown in the button list vary depending on the scanner model.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	If you use Button Event Manager to specify an image scanning application for the scan button on a scanner, take note of the following.	When PaperStream ClickScan is running	Regardless of any settings that were configured for the scan button with Button Event Manager, a scan is performed with PaperStream ClickScan when the scan button on a scanner is pressed.	To start up another image scanning application (by pressing the scan button on a scanner), exit PaperStream ClickScan. For details, refer to the PaperStream ClickScan Help.	When PaperStream ClickScan is not running and PaperStream Capture is installed	PaperStream Capture is automatically set for the scan button on a scanner.	If you do not set PaperStream Capture for the scan button on a scanner, select [Take no action] or [Run the following program] in [Operation].	For details about how to set a button on the scanner, refer to 	Configuring the Settings for Buttons on a Scanner.	Operation 	Launch [PaperStream Capture] 	Select this to start PaperStream Capture.	Document profile names are displayed on the touch screen or the operator panel depending on the scanner that you use.	For details, refer to the PaperStream Capture Help.	Run the following program 	Select this to run a program of your choice.	Specify the path of a program to run.	[Browse] button 	Displays the [Select an application] window.	Specify a program to run.	Parameters 	Up to 255 characters can be specified for parameters.	For details about parameters, refer to the manual of the program to run.	Take no action 	Select this to not run any program.	[OK] button 	Closes the window.	The changes are saved.	[Cancel] button 	Closes the window.	The changes are not saved.'];
searchDatas1[39] = ['','Error Messages','./title_tb.html', '	Error Messages	This section describes error messages that may be displayed while you are using Network Setup Tool for fi Series and explains the solutions for the errors. 	Scanner Selection Tool	IP Address Setting Tool	Certificate Registration Tool	Button Event Manager	'];
searchDatas1[40] = ['','Scanner Selection Tool','./tb_select.html', '	Scanner Selection Tool	This section describes error messages that may be displayed while you are using Scanner Selection Tool and explains the solutions for the errors. 	Failed to modify the configuration file.	Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.	Invalid IP address. Enter a correct IP address.	Failed to load the configuration file.	Failed to start up the program.	No help file is found.	The name is incorrect. Enter the correct name.	'];
searchDatas1[41] = ['','Failed to modify the configuration file.','./tb_select_01.html', '	Failed to modify the configuration file.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	Creating a configuration file or writing in the configuration file is not possible	Obtaining the path to the configuration file failed	Another application is accessing the configuration file	Solution 	Exit all the applications that are running and then restart Scanner Selection Tool.'];
searchDatas1[42] = ['','Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.','./tb_select_03.html', '	Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.	Cause 	An unexpected error occurred.	Solution 	Restart the computer and then restart Scanner Selection Tool.'];
searchDatas1[43] = ['','Invalid IP address. Enter a correct IP address.','./tb_select_04.html', '	Invalid IP address. Enter a correct IP address.	Cause 	The IP address that you entered is incorrect.	Solution 	For fi-8040 or fi-7300NX	Check the IP address on the touch screen of the scanner and enter the correct IP address.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250	Use IP Address Setting Tool to check the IP address of the scanner and enter the correct IP address.	For details about how to start IP Address Setting Tool, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.'];
searchDatas1[44] = ['','Failed to load the configuration file.','./tb_select_05.html', '	Failed to load the configuration file.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	You have no access privileges to the configuration file	Obtaining the path to the configuration file failed	Another application is accessing the configuration file	Solution 	Exit all the applications that are running and then restart Scanner Selection Tool.'];
searchDatas1[45] = ['','Failed to start up the program.','./tb_select_06.html', '	Failed to start up the program.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	An error has occurred on the computer	There is no executable file for IP Address Setting Tool	Solution 	Perform the following:	Restart the computer.	Uninstall Network Setup Tool for fi Series, and then install it again.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[46] = ['','No help file is found.','./tb_select_07.html', '	No help file is found.	Cause 	The help file does not exist.	Solution 	Uninstall Network Setup Tool for fi Series, and then install it again.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[47] = ['','The name is incorrect. Enter the correct name.','./tb_select_08.html', '	The name is incorrect. Enter the correct name.	Cause 	The name of the scanner is incorrect.	Solution 	Enter the correct name.	The following characters are available:	Alphanumeric characters	- (Hyphen)	. (Period)	Up to 255 characters can be entered.'];
searchDatas1[48] = ['','IP Address Setting Tool','./tb_ip.html', '	IP Address Setting Tool	This section describes error messages that may be displayed while you are using IP Address Setting Tool and explains the solutions for the errors. 	Connect the scanner to the computer using the USB cable.	Connect only one scanner.	A communication error occurred.	Unsupported characters are included in the scanner name.	A reserved address cannot be specified for the IP Address.	A reserved address cannot be specified for the subnet mask.	The IP address or subnet mask is invalid.	The IP address is in an incorrect format.	The subnet prefix length is in an incorrect format.	A reserved address cannot be specified for the default gateway.	The default gateway is in an incorrect format.	The default gateway or subnet mask is invalid.	A scanner name has not been entered.	This scanner is being used by another user or application.	Failed to start up the program.	Login failed.	No help file is found.	'];
searchDatas1[49] = ['','Connect the scanner to the computer using the USB cable.','./tb_ip_01.html', '	Connect the scanner to the computer using the USB cable.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	The scanner is not connected to the computer with the USB cable	The scanner driver has not been installed	The scanner is not turned on	The scanner that is connected to the computer is not supported by IP Address Setting Tool	Solution 	Perform the following:	Connect the scanner to the computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner.	Install the scanner driver.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Turn on the scanner.	Check which scanner models are supported by IP Address Setting Tool.	For details, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.'];
searchDatas1[50] = ['','Connect only one scanner.','./tb_ip_02.html', '	Connect only one scanner.	Cause 	Multiple scanners are connected to the computer.	Solution 	Connect only one scanner when connecting a scanner to the computer with the USB cable.'];
searchDatas1[51] = ['','A communication error occurred.','./tb_ip_03.html', '	A communication error occurred.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	An error occurred during communication with the scanner	An operation was carried out when the scanner was in the middle of the initialization process	The network function of the scanner is disabled 	Solution 	Perform the following:	Turn the scanner off then back on.	Check that the initialization of the scanner is completed.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Start up Software Operation Panel to enable the network function.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[52] = ['','Unsupported characters are included in the scanner name.','./tb_ip_04.html', '	Unsupported characters are included in the scanner name.	Cause 	Characters that cannot be used for the scanner name have been set.	Solution 	Check the characters that have been set for the scanner name.	Available characters are alphanumeric characters, "-" (hyphen), "_" (underscore), and spaces.'];
searchDatas1[53] = ['','A reserved address cannot be specified for the IP Address.','./tb_ip_05.html', '	A reserved address cannot be specified for the IP Address.	Cause 	An invalid IP address has been set.	Solution 	Enter a correct IP address.	For an IPv4 address	Each xxx in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx should be a value from 0 to 255.	Check the following and then try again.	The values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the scanner	For an IPv6 address	Each xxxx in xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx should be a value from 0 to ffff.	Check the following and then try again.	The values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the scanner'];
searchDatas1[54] = ['','A reserved address cannot be specified for the subnet mask.','./tb_ip_06.html', '	A reserved address cannot be specified for the subnet mask.	Cause 	An invalid subnet mask has been set.	Solution 	Enter a valid subnet mask.	Each xxx in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx should be a value from 0 to 255.	Check the following and then try again.	The values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the subnet mask'];
searchDatas1[55] = ['','The IP address or subnet mask is invalid.','./tb_ip_07.html', '	The IP address or subnet mask is invalid.	Cause 	An invalid IP address or subnet mask has been set.	Solution 	Enter a valid IP address or subnet mask.	Each xxx in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx should be a value from 0 to 255.	Check that the values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the scanner or the subnet mask, and then try again.'];
searchDatas1[56] = ['','The IP address is in an incorrect format.','./tb_ip_18.html', '	The IP address is in an incorrect format.	Cause 	The IP address for IPv6 is in an incorrect format.	Solution 	Enter the IP address in the correct format.	Each xxxx in xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx should be a value from 0 to ffff.	Check the following and then try again.	A value in a hexadecimal number is entered in the input fields	A shortened form (::) is used less than twice	There are no blanks in the input fields'];
searchDatas1[57] = ['','The subnet prefix length is in an incorrect format.','./tb_ip_16.html', '	The subnet prefix length is in an incorrect format.	Cause 	The subnet prefix length for an IPv6 address is in an incorrect format.	Solution 	Enter the subnet prefix length in the correct format.	A value from 3 to 128 can be entered.'];
searchDatas1[58] = ['','A reserved address cannot be specified for the default gateway.','./tb_ip_09.html', '	A reserved address cannot be specified for the default gateway.	Cause 	An invalid default gateway has been set.	Solution 	Enter a valid default gateway.	For an IPv4 address	Each xxx in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx should be a value from 0 to 255.	Check the following and then try again.	The values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the default gateway	For an IPv6 address	Each xxxx in xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx should be a value from 0 to ffff.	Check the following and then try again.	The values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the default gateway'];
searchDatas1[59] = ['','The default gateway is in an incorrect format.','./tb_ip_19.html', '	The default gateway is in an incorrect format.	Cause 	The default gateway for IPv6 is in an incorrect format.	Solution 	Enter the default gateway in the correct format.	Each xxxx in xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx should be a value from 0 to ffff.	Check the following and then try again.	A value in a hexadecimal number is entered in the input fields	A shortened form (::) is used less than twice'];
searchDatas1[60] = ['','The default gateway or subnet mask is invalid.','./tb_ip_10.html', '	The default gateway or subnet mask is invalid.	Cause 	An invalid default gateway or subnet mask has been set.	Solution 	Enter a valid default gateway or subnet mask.	Each xxx in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx should be a value from 0 to 255.	Check that the values you input are the same as the ones assigned to the default gateway or the subnet mask, and then try again.'];
searchDatas1[61] = ['','A scanner name has not been entered.','./tb_ip_14.html', '	A scanner name has not been entered.	Cause 	A scanner name has not been entered.	Solution 	Enter one or more characters in the [Scanner Name] input field.	Available characters are alphanumeric characters, "-" (hyphen), "_" (underscore), and spaces.'];
searchDatas1[62] = ['','This scanner is being used by another user or application.','./tb_ip_12.html', '	This scanner is being used by another user or application.	Cause 	Another application or another user is using the scanner.	Solution 	Make sure that the other application or user is not using the scanner.	Also, exit the application that is using the scanner.	If the problem persists, turn the scanner off then back on.'];
searchDatas1[63] = ['','Failed to start up the program.','./tb_ip_13.html', '	Failed to start up the program.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	An error has occurred on the computer	There is no executable file for Scanner Selection Tool	Solution 	Perform the following:	Restart the computer.	Uninstall Network Setup Tool for fi Series, and then install it again.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[64] = ['','Login failed.','./tb_ip_17.html', '	Login failed.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	The password that you entered is different from the administrator password for the scanner	An error has occurred in the scanner	Solution 	Perform the following:	Enter the correct administrator password for the scanner.	Turn the scanner off then back on.'];
searchDatas1[65] = ['','No help file is found.','./tb_ip_15.html', '	No help file is found.	Cause 	The help file does not exist.	Solution 	Uninstall Network Setup Tool for fi Series, and then install it again.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[66] = ['','Certificate Registration Tool','./tb_cer.html', '	Certificate Registration Tool	This section describes error messages that may be displayed while you are using Certificate Registration Tool and explains the solutions for the errors. 	Failed to connect to the scanner.	Failed to obtain certificate information.	Failed to remove the certificate.	Failed to register the certificate.	Incorrect password.	'];
searchDatas1[67] = ['','Failed to connect to the scanner.','./tb_cer_01.html', '	Failed to connect to the scanner.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	The scanner is not turned on	The scanner is not connected to the computer with the USB cable	The scanner is in the middle of the start-up process	The scanner settings are being changed	Multiple scanners are connected to the computer	Another application is using the scanner	The scanner that is connected to the computer is not supported by Certificate Registration Tool	Solution 	Perform the following:	Turn on the scanner.	Connect the scanner to the computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner.	Check that the scanner is not in the middle of the start-up process.	Finish changing the scanner settings.	Connect only one scanner to the computer.	Exit the other application that is using the scanner.	Check which scanner models are supported by Certificate Registration Tool.	For details, refer to 	Supported Scanner Models.	If a message is still displayed after taking measures above, perform the following:	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again.	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.	Restart the computer.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.'];
searchDatas1[68] = ['','Failed to obtain certificate information.','./tb_cer_02.html', '	Failed to obtain certificate information.	Cause 	You performed the following after clicking the [Set] button in the 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window.	Turning off the scanner	Connecting and disconnecting the scanner to the computer with the USB cable	Solution 	Perform the following:	Turn on the scanner.	Connect the scanner to the computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.	If a message is still displayed after taking measures above, perform the following:	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again.	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.	Restart the computer.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.'];
searchDatas1[69] = ['','Failed to remove the certificate.','./tb_cer_04.html', '	Failed to remove the certificate.	Cause 	You performed the following after clicking the [Set] button in the 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window.	Turning off the scanner	Connecting and disconnecting the scanner to the computer with the USB cable	Solution 	Perform the following:	Turn on the scanner.	Connect the scanner to the computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.	If a message is still displayed after taking measures above, perform the following:	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again.	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.	Restart the computer.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.'];
searchDatas1[70] = ['','Failed to register the certificate.','./tb_cer_05.html', '	Failed to register the certificate.	Cause 	The issue may be caused by the following:	The format of the specified certificate is not correct	Loading the specified certificate failed	You performed the following after clicking the [Set] button in the 	[Certificate Registration Tool] Window	Turning off the scanner	Connecting and disconnecting the scanner to the computer with the USB cable	Solution 	Perform the following:	Check that the format of the certificate is correct.	Certificates that can be registered are as follows:	Client certificate: PKCS#12 format file (*.p12, *.pfx)	CA certificate: CA certificate file (*.cer, *.crt, *.der, *.pem)	Check that you have access privileges to the certificate file.	Turn on the scanner.	Connect the scanner to the computer with the USB cable that is supplied with the scanner.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.	If a message is still displayed after taking measures above, perform the following:	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again.	TIP	When you try to turn off the scanner, the message "Operating..." may keep appearing on the touch screen of the scanner. Even if this occurs, turning off the scanner should not be a problem.	Restart the computer.	Restart Certificate Registration Tool.'];
searchDatas1[71] = ['','Incorrect password.','./tb_cer_06.html', '	Incorrect password.	Cause 	The password that you entered is incorrect.	Solution 	Enter the correct password.	The following characters can be used for the password.	Alphanumeric characters	A to Z, a to z, 0 to 9	Symbols	! " # $ % & \' ( ) * + , - . / : ; < = > ? @ [ 	\\ ] ^ _ ` { | } ~	Spaces'];
searchDatas1[72] = ['','Button Event Manager','./tb_bem.html', '	Button Event Manager	This section describes error messages that may be displayed while you are using Button Event Manager and explains the solutions for the errors. 	Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.	No help file is found.	'];
searchDatas1[73] = ['','Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.','./tb_bem_01.html', '	Failed to process because an unexpected error occurred.	Cause 	An unexpected error occurred.	Solution 	Restart the computer and then restart Button Event Manager.'];
searchDatas1[74] = ['','No help file is found.','./tb_bem_02.html', '	No help file is found.	Cause 	The help file does not exist.	Solution 	Uninstall Network Setup Tool for fi Series, and then install it again.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
searchDatas1[75] = ['','Troubleshooting','./title_trouble.html', '	Troubleshooting	This section describes troubles that may occur while you are using Network Setup Tool for fi Series and explains the solutions for the troubles. 	No Scanner Is Found	Cannot Perform a Scan by Pressing the Button on the Scanner	'];
searchDatas1[76] = ['','No Scanner Is Found','./trouble_01.html', '	No Scanner Is Found	Check the following: 	Is the connection method (used to connect the scanner) different from the one that is set in the scanner settings? (fi-7300NX)	Are the scanner\'s network settings configured properly?	Is the scanner in the middle of the start-up process or the initialization process?	Is another application using the scanner?	Are the computer\'s network settings configured properly?	Is the operating system on the computer being updated or waiting to be restarted?	Is the scanner connected to the same subnetwork as your computer?	Are the settings for network devices (such as a switch, hub, or router) correct?	Is the communication status between the scanner and the computer stable?	If a scanner is not found after taking the measures above, restart the scanner and computer and then restart Scanner Selection Tool.	If a scanner does not appear in the image scanning application, refer to 	Cannot Perform a Scan from the Image Scanning Application.	Is the connection method (used to connect the scanner) different from the one that is set in the scanner settings? (fi-7300NX)	Solution 	Check that Wi-Fi or a wired LAN is set for the connection method of the scanner.	You can check it as follows.	On the touch screen of the scanner, press 	 	→ [Scanner Settings] 	→ [How to connect].	Are the scanner\'s network settings configured properly?	Solution 	For fi-8040 or fi-7300NX	Check the network settings of the scanner.	You can check it as follows.	On the touch screen of the scanner, press 	 	→ [Scanner Settings] 	→ [Network].	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250	Use IP Address Setting Tool to check the network settings of the scanner.	For details about how to start IP Address Setting Tool, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.	Is the scanner in the middle of the start-up process or the initialization process?	Solution 	Check that the scanner is not in the middle of the start-up process or the initialization process.	For details, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.	Is another application using the scanner?	Solution 	Exit the other application that is using the scanner.	Are the computer\'s network settings configured properly?	Solution 	Check the computer\'s network settings.	For details about how to configure the computer\'s network settings, refer to the manual of your computer.	Is the operating system on the computer being updated or waiting to be restarted?	Solution 	Restart Scanner Selection Tool after the operating system on the computer is updated or the computer is restarted.	Is the scanner connected to the same subnetwork as your computer?	Even if the scanner is connected to the same subnetwork as your computer, it may not be found.	Solution 	Select [Search from the IP address of the scanner] in the 	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window and enter the IP address to search for the scanner.	Are the settings for network devices (such as a switch, hub, or router) correct?	Solution 	Check the settings for network devices (such as a switch, hub, or router).	For details about how to set the network device, refer to the manual of your network device.	Is the communication status between the scanner and the computer stable?	Solution 	For fi-8040 or fi-7300NX	Check the communication status between the scanner and the computer.	You can check the communication status between the scanner and the computer on the touch screen of the scanner.	You can check it as follows.	On the touch screen of the scanner, press 	 	→ [Scanner Settings] 	→ [Network] 	→ [Check connection (Ping)].	For fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, or fi-8250	Check the communication status between the scanner and the computer.	Start up the command prompt on your computer, and execute the ping command to check the communication status by specifying the IP address for the scanner.	Use IP Address Setting Tool to check the IP address for the scanner.	For details about how to start IP Address Setting Tool, refer to 	Starting Up IP Address Setting Tool.'];
searchDatas1[77] = ['','Cannot Perform a Scan by Pressing the Button on the Scanner','./trouble_02.html', '	Cannot Perform a Scan by Pressing the Button on the Scanner	Check the following: 	Is the scanner selected in Scanner Selection Tool?	Has Button Event Manager been started?	Is [Watch Button Event] selected on the menu of Button Event Manager?	Is the settings for the button on the scanner correct?	Is the scanner being used by another computer?	Is the scanner selected in Scanner Selection Tool?	Solution 	In the 	[Scanner Selection Tool] Window, check that the scanner is selected.	Has Button Event Manager been started?	Solution 	Check that Button Event Manager has been started.	When Button Event Manager has been started, 	 appears in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar.	For details about how to start Button Event Manager, refer to 	Starting Up Button Event Manager.	Is [Watch Button Event] selected on the menu of Button Event Manager?	Solution 	Start Button Event Manager and right-click 	 in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar to display the 	Menu of Button Event Manager. Check that [Watch Button Event] is selected.	For details about how to start Button Event Manager, refer to 	Starting Up Button Event Manager.	Is the settings for the button on the scanner correct?	Solution 	In the 	[Button Settings] Window of Button Event Manager, check that the button setting is correct.	Check that the image scanning application that you specified for the button on the scanner runs on the computer.	Is the scanner being used by another computer?	Solution 	When the same scanner has been selected by more than one computer using Scanner Selection Tool, select [Watch Button Event] on the menu of Button Event Manager only on the computer that you want to use the scanner with.	If you cannot start a scan after taking the measures above, perform the following:	Exit the image scanning application which resides in the notification area located at the far right of the task bar	Turn off the scanner and turn it on again'];
searchDatas1[78] = ['','Supported Scanner Models','./support.html', '	Supported Scanner Models	The scanner models supported by Network Setup Tool for fi Series are as follows. 	Scanner Selection Tool	fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8040, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, fi-8250, fi-7300NX	IP Address Setting Tool	fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, fi-8250	Certificate Registration Tool	fi-7300NX	Button Event Manager	fi-8950, fi-8930, fi-8820, fi-8040, fi-8190, fi-8290, fi-8170, fi-8270, fi-8150, fi-8250, fi-7300NX'];
searchDatas1[79] = ['','Cannot Perform a Scan from the Image Scanning Application','./trouble_04.html', '	Cannot Perform a Scan from the Image Scanning Application	Check the following: 	Has a proxy server been set for the WinHTTP proxy setting?	Has a proxy server been set for the WinHTTP proxy setting?	Solution 	Change the WinHTTP proxy settings so that you can access the scanner from the computer.	Change the WinHTTP proxy settings in the following procedure.	Start up the command prompt window as a user with Administrator privileges on the computer.	Run the following command to check the proxy server name and port numbers that are to be used.	netsh winhttp show proxy	TIP	The proxy server name and port numbers that are to be used will be displayed as follows.	"Proxy server name: Port numbers"	Run one of the following commands.	When a proxy server has already been set	Configure the setting so that the computer can access the scanner without the use of the proxy server.	netsh winhttp set proxy proxy-server="XXXXXX:YYYY" bypass-list=ZZZ.ZZZ.ZZZ.ZZZ	XXXXXX: Proxy server name	YYYY: Port numbers to be used	ZZZ.ZZZ.ZZZ.ZZZ: IP address of the scanner (*1)(*2)	When the proxy server has not been set	If you reset the settings, the computer may be able to access the scanner.	netsh winhttp reset proxy	*1:	You can check the IP address of a scanner on the touch screen or the operator panel of the scanner or in IP Address Setting Tool.	*2:	The IPv4 address format is used as an example here.	For an IPv6 address, the following format is used.	ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ:ZZZZ'];
searchDatas1[80] = ['','Administrator Password for a Scanner','./adminpassword.html', '	Administrator Password for a Scanner	For details about the factory default administrator password, refer to the Operator\'s Guide of the scanner.'];
